+## The widescreen patch list
+
+The mods of the title folders come from "Widescreen patches for Xbox
+Original" (ps2wide.wordpress.com/xbox): its "initial value" and "change to"
+are the two sides of a `find` line. A headline of the list is a mod
+(`Widescreen`, `Cutscenes letterbox fix`, `FMV's fix`), and the parts under
+it (`value 1`, `value 2`) are the lines of that mod; parts with no headline
+above them are the `Widescreen`. A label such as "(2 times)" is how many
+places the bytes are in the XBE: `find[2]`, which makes the patch only
+when it finds exactly that many (another release of the game doesn't).
+Left out: Need for Speed: Hot Pursuit 2's `inis.viv` (a data file, not the
+XBE), and TRON 2.0's, whose patches are for `TRON20KA.xbe` (the app patches
+`default.xbe` only).
